      "note": "try_emit takes no model, key or network: with verify=None it runs six emitters, applies the emit-blocking conformance rules in-process and returns RTL or (None, None). The AI is the BACKUP arm and its absence degrades the ANSWER, never the mechanism -- an unrecognised prompt reports WAIVED naming the fallback skill, a stated handover rather than a silent pass. The refusal half is pinned too: a solver outside its envelope returns None rather than guessing, so an unavailable AI cannot be papered over by a program emitting something wrong."
